     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">I have two components to a problem that I am inexperienced with.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">I am trying to use a shiny interface to render a table:</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(36,39,41)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\">  renderTable({table(do_something(rownames(datset)[which(dataset$covariate&gt;input$tab)]))})\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">That works fine but the problem is that the factor I have to make this statement multiple times for a number of different elements for which the measurements are different. i.e. the some range from 0-4 and others from 0-20. The slider that I have selected has a range of 0-10 so in the case of measurements ranging from 0-4 when I select a slider value greater than 4 I will get the following error.</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(36,39,41)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\">  Error:subscript out of bounds\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://i.stack.imgur.com/q3LXs.png\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,89,153)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://i.stack.imgur.com/q3LXs.png&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792393316175000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0eRtSDbkzFJBBgW5ZBfq-T\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/gsVgEtU5ieVGS0vQ_EjJraLkJvqFHXC6aK59MqNYlHwsO1eHK5M6fSapUJNkgfoBcLcO5DE=s0-d-e1-ft#http://i.stack.imgur.com/q3LXs.png\" alt=\"enter image description here\" style=\"max-width:100%\"></a></p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">I need to be able to return a message to the GUI interface explaining why the error is happening to the user, rather than having an uninformative Error message appear.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">My attempt to do this is as follows:</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(36,39,41)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\">  renderTable({try(table(do_something(rownames(datset)[which(dataset$covariate&gt;input$tab)])))})\r\n  options(show.error.messages=F)\r\n  validate(\r\nneed(input$data != &quot;&quot;, &quot;Maximum for this measurement has been reached&quot;)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">)</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">but I get the following error:</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(36,39,41)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\">Error in .getReactiveEnvironment()$currentContext() : \r\nOperation not allowed without an active reactive context. (You tried to do something that can only be done from inside a reactive expression or observer.)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">I am inexperienced with error handling both in R and in shiny so I am looking for a good example of an expression that just anticipates a specific error and allows me to return a personalised message to the user... I have researched the command &#39;tryCatch&#39; but it doesn&#39;t seem to have the flexibility that I need....</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Thanks in advance</p></div>"
